# Coach speech (Japanese): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang.
#
# Register: polite です/ます style, always positive, never blaming; short noun-ending sentences
# (体言止め) at levels 5-6. The coach is 私.
# Placeholders (see the English header): {move} a move (a noun phrase in speech: "ナイト・エフさん");
# {n:moveno} / {crit_no:moveno} / {k:moveno} a move NUMBER, "11手目" (count.moveno in common.lang);
# {moves:move} "24手"; {n:piece} "駒3個"; {m:time} "2回"; {pts:point} "3点";
# {acc:percent} "75%" (spoken "ななじゅうごパーセント", count.percent); {n:mistake} "1回のミス" ...
# {text} = a phase (appraisal.phase.*, a noun: "中盤") or a draw reason (appraisal.reason.*, an
# adverbial phrase read before "引き分け": "ステイルメイトで引き分け"); {theme} = a theme.* phrase
# (a nominal "〜こと" phrase, said after "練習するといいこと："); {level} = a level name, said in
# 「」 ("「中級者」に進めそうです"). A ".spoken" key respells digits and chess kanji in kana.

